{
  "_id": "tg-jerusalem",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Melchizedek king of Salem brought forth bread, Gen. 14:18. Jebusites dwell … at Jerusalem, Josh. 15:63 (Judg. 1:21). Judah had fought against Jerusalem, Judg. 1:8. king … went to Jerusalem, 2 Sam. 5:6 (1 Chr. 11:4). Assyria sent … great host against Jerusalem, 2 Kgs. 18:17 (Isa. 36:2). Nebuchadnezzar … came up against Jerusalem, 2 Kgs. 24:10. Chaldees … brake down the walls of Jerusalem, 2 Kgs. 25:10 (2 Chr. 36:19; Jer. 52:14). charged me to build him an house in Jerusalem, 2 Chr. 36:23 (Ezra 1:2). how Jerusalem lieth waste … build up the wall of Jerusalem, Neh. 2:17. build thou the walls of Jerusalem, Ps. 51:18. thou shalt be called, The city of righteousness, Isa. 1:26. he that remaineth in Jerusalem, shall be called holy, Isa. 4:3. they call themselves of the holy city, Isa. 48:2 (1 Ne. 20:2). put on thy beautiful garments, O Jerusalem, Isa. 52:1. till he make Jerusalem a praise in the earth, Isa. 62:7. Jerusalem the throne of the Lord, Jer. 3:17. Jerusalem shall become heaps, Jer. 26:18 (Micah 3:12). all his army against Jerusalem, and they besieged it, Jer. 39:1. cause Jerusalem to know her abominations, Ezek. 16:2. said against Jerusalem, Aha, she is broken, Ezek. 26:2. saying, The city is smitten, Ezek. 33:21. fury be turned away from thy city Jerusalem, Dan. 9:16. in Jerusalem shall be deliverance, Joel 2:32. then shall Jerusalem be holy, Joel 3:17. word of the Lord from Jerusalem, Micah 4:2. Jerusalem shall be called a city of truth, Zech. 8:3. Jerusalem shall be inhabited again, Zech. 12:6. will gather all nations against Jerusalem to battle, Zech. 14:2.",
