    {
      "text": "Jerusalem … city of the great King, Matt. 5:35. we go up to Jerusalem, Matt. 20:18 (Mark 10:32; Luke 18:31). Jerusalem, thou that killest the prophets, Matt. 23:37 (23:37–39; Luke 13:34). abomination of desolation … stand in the holy place, Matt. 24:15 (JS—M 1:12). brought him to Jerusalem, to present him to the Lord, Luke 2:22. he was twelve years old, they went up to Jerusalem, Luke 2:42. see Jerusalem compassed with armies, Luke 21:20. Jerusalem shall be trodden down of the Gentiles, Luke 21:24. Daughters of Jerusalem, weep not for me, Luke 23:28. be preached in his name … beginning at Jerusalem, Luke 24:47. great persecution against the church … at Jerusalem, Acts 8:1. went up to Jerusalem to see Peter, Gal. 1:18. Jerusalem which is above is free, Gal. 4:26. King of Salem, which is, King of peace, Heb. 7:2. city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, Heb. 12:22.",
